### Description

Switch an existing cron job on or off. A newly created cron job is paused by default and only starts to be triggered as planned after this API switches it on; once paused, the cron job is removed from the scheduler and is no longer triggered.

Before calling: the target cron job must exist in the given resource scope and the caller must have the permission to switch cron jobs on and off in that resource scope. Switching a cron job on additionally requires the permission to launch the job plan it uses.

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| id | long | Yes | Cron job ID, must be a positive integer |
| status | int | Yes | Target status. Options: 1 (switch on), 2 (pause) |

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "id": 700001,
    "status": 1
}
```

